  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "The largest army in the Arab world: a conscript mass army with a mix of US-supplied armour (M1A1 Abrams co-produced in Egypt, M60A3, M113) and Soviet-legacy, Chinese, Russian, French and Korean equipment. Its main combat experience since 2013 is counter-insurgency against the ISIS Sinai Province in northern Sinai (largely suppressed by 2023), plus border security on the Gaza (Rafah), Libyan and Sudanese frontiers. Egypt keeps a peace treaty with Israel, mediates in Gaza and contributes troops to the African Union mission in Somalia (AUSSOM). Doctrine is heavy on armour, artillery and fixed checkpoints; quality varies widely between conscript units and elite formations (Thunderbolt/Sa'ka commandos, Unit 777, Republican Guard).",
    "squad_size": 9,
    "fireteam": "Infantry squad of 9-11 conscripts around a PKM and RPG-7, carried in M113, Fahd or BMP-1; Sa'ka (Thunderbolt) commando teams of 6-10. In game: 8 men in battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Fortified checkpoints and berms along roads and borders (Sinai, Rafah)",
      "Armoured columns with Abrams/M60 and M113 sweeping villages after air and artillery preparation",
      "Commando raids and cordon-and-search operations against insurgent cells",
      "Apache gunships and Wing Loong drones for close support in the desert",
      "Engineer demolition of tunnels and creation of buffer zones on the Gaza border"
    ],
